PVD("papua_new_guinea_ndp_2016-2017",{"docs":["","PNG NDP 2016 17"],"s":{"1":[[1,"57","12","Strategic Water and Gas-Based Power Development","The abundance of the strategic assets of water and gas must be considered as a basis of cheaper power for domestic consumption and export as prescribed by StaRS.",""],[1,"57","14","Standalone Sustainable Township Power Generation Systems","It is desired that provincial and district townships establish standalone, sustainable power generation systems where possible.",""],[1,"57","14","Biogas Electricity Generation for Agricultural Processing Projects","Large-scale agricultural projects with processing systems such as the oil palm industry lend itself to biogas electricity generation at sustainable and cheap rates.",""],[1,"58","1","Electricity Generation and Distribution Capacity Improvement Projects","The Government is funding a range of projects with the intention of improving generation and distribution capacity.",""],[1,"58","2","MTDP2 Investment Continuation","The Government will continue this investment under MTDP2.",""],[1,"72","3","National Household Electricity Access Expansion","MTDP2 will continue the process begun by MTDP1 on increasing access to electricity for all households in the country but with greater focus on the generation and supply from cleaner sources of energy.",""],[1,"72","6","Regional Grid Expansion and Maintenance Programme","Ongoing work on the set up of regional grids will continue as part of the strategy to provide access nationwide.",""],[1,"72","6","National Grid Consolidation and Interconnection Initiative","The consolidation of regional grids into a national grid should provide for potential international connection and export to Eastern Australia.",""]],"2":[[1,"72","2","Clean Energy Development","This has to be reversed and cleaner energy sources need to be developed.",""],[1,"72","3","Cleaner Energy Transition for Power Generation","Generating electricity from gas to meet growing demand is necessary in the medium term but commitment by Government is needed to shift away from fossil fuel reliance and towards cleaner sources of energy.",""],[1,"72","4","Research and Development on Cleaner Energy Sources","Greater understanding through research and development is needed on the cost and effectiveness of alternative sources of cleaner power such as bio-fuel, hydro, geothermal, biomass, wind and solar.",""],[1,"72","4","Investment in Alternative Cleaner Energy Generation and Distribution","This will guide increased investments in the generation and distribution of alternative cleaner sources of energy.",""],[1,"72","4","Bio-fuel Assessment for Transport Sector","For the transport sector, bio-fuel will be assessed as a low cost cleaner alternative to diesel.",""],[1,"72","5","Independent Power Producer Market Opening","Power generation needs to be opened to independent power producers in order to increase both the amount of electricity generated and the share of renewable energy in the national energy mix.",""],[1,"72","5","Power Sector Restructuring and Unbundling Reform","Restructuring of the sector by separating generation, transmission and distribution services can have a significant effect on electric power technologies, costs, prices, institutions, and regulatory frameworks, and can create more space for renewable and clean energy in the national energy mix.",""],[1,"72","14","Clean Renewable Energy Expansion","It is anticipated that the proportion of energy/electricity produced from clean renewable energy sources such as hydro, solar, wind, tidal, geo-thermal, biomass and biogas will be increased.",""],[1,"72","14","Reduction of Wood Fuel and Slash-and-Burn Use","The use of wood for cooking and slash and burn in agriculture will also be reduced.",""]],"3":[[1,"27","3","Small and Medium Enterprise Investment Support","Chapter four sets out the strategic direction for growing the economy - focused on the critical activities of investing in small and medium enterprises and re-positioning PNGs strategic assets.",""],[1,"65","6","SME Policy and Legislative Framework","This includes a robust SME policy and establishing the necessary legislative framework to guide and grow the sector.",""],[1,"65","6","Small Business Capacity-Building Training Support","It has also started to build small business capacity through support for training programs such as Know About Business and Start, Improve Business.",""],[1,"65","9","Support for Emerging SMEs under MTDP2","The Government will continue to encourage emerging SMEs under MTDP2.",""],[1,"65","10","SME Market Access and Credit Support","Continuing to improve SMEs access to markets and financial credit;",""],[1,"65","12","Informal Economy Formalization and SME Transition Support","Encouraging the operation of the informal economy and streamlining the transition process for SMEs from the informal to the formal economy;",""]],"4":[[1,"73","2","World-Class Mining Project Development","Several new world-class mining projects are nearing completion of feasibility studies and are expected to begin construction and production within the medium term.",""],[1,"73","5","State Institution Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of state institutions responsible for policy, administration, regulation, compliance and enforcement;",""],[1,"73","7","Restrictions on New Mineral Exploration","Maximizing exploration in existing tenements whilst placing restrictions on new explorations;",""],[1,"73","10","Community Relocation and Mining Environmental Management Policies","Developing policies for the relocation of affected communities, effective mine waste management, responsible seabed mining and downstream processing; and",""]],"5":[[1,"69","13","Economic Corridor Utilization for Agricultural Development","Utilization of Economic Corridors for agricultural development",""]],"6":[[1,"37","10","Responsive Financial Services Sector Policy","Under the MTDP2 the Government's financial services sector policy will be responsive to the need of the public and private sector and individuals at all levels of society.",""],[1,"37","12","Financial Services for Transparent Revenue Transfer Management","Utilizing the financial services sector to improve transparency, security and accountability of revenue transfers between levels of government and to other beneficiaries;",""],[1,"37","13","Financial Inclusion for Low-Income Citizens and Small Businesses","Providing low income citizens, micro and small businesses access to a diverse range of financial products and services;",""],[1,"37","14","Capital Market Access Policy Development","Developing policies that encourage greater access to capital markets for public and private sector investors.",""],[1,"38","3","Private Sector Capital Access Expansion","Expanding the private sector's access to capital, especially for investment in the construction, agriculture, extractive, and manufacturing industries;",""],[1,"38","4","Development of Financial Products for Small Enterprises and Start-ups","Developing new financial products that meet the demands of small enterprises and start-up companies that struggle to secure investment funds from commercial banks;",""],[1,"38","5","Banking Sector Innovation for Cost Reduction","Encouraging innovation from the banking sector to reduce transaction and overhead costs;",""],[1,"38","6","Financial Services Development Support for Private Individuals","Continuing support for the development of financial services to private individuals through micro finance and other facilities.",""]],"8":[[1,"64","5","Smallholder Agriculture Mobilization and Productivity Improvement","the Government is required to develop better systems to mobilize land, organise farmers, create nucleus estates, improve productivity, efficiency and also to encourage entrepreneurship and development of small to medium enterprises as vehicles for participation in this effort.",""],[1,"69","2","Rural Infrastructure and Market Access Support","Enablers such as roads, bridges, extension service, access to markets, with appropriate regulatory policies will enable the sector to grow.",""],[1,"69","8","Key Supply Chain Development","Development of key supply chains to link producers to markets;",""],[1,"69","9","Agricultural Extension Services Provision","Provision of appropriate extension services;",""],[1,"69","10","Pest, Disease, and Climate Change Coping and Mitigation Strategy Development","Development of coping and mitigation strategies for pests and diseases and climate change;",""],[1,"69","11","Research and Development Funding","Funding of research and development;",""],[1,"69","12","Enforcement of CODEX Marketing Standards","Enforcement of CODEX marketing standards;",""]],"9":[[1,"68","1","In-Country Tuna Processing Expansion","The Government's long-term objective is to attain 100% in country processing of the tuna catch from within its EEZ.",""],[1,"68","4","Sustainable Marine Resource Plan","Reviewing, developing and implementing a Sustainable Marine Resource plan;",""],[1,"68","5","Responsible Fisheries and Marine Resource Awareness Campaign","Creating awareness on responsible management and use of fishery and marine resources;",""],[1,"68","6","Combating and Monitoring of Illegal, Unreported and Unregulated Fishing","Combating and monitoring of illegal unreported unregulated fishing;",""],[1,"68","7","Restricted Licensing System","Introducing a restricted licensing system;",""],[1,"68","8","Fisheries Authority Human Capital and Institutional Capacity Development","Developing the human capital and institutional capacity for the National Fisheries Authority and related stakeholders of the fishery sector.",""],[1,"68","11","Recreational and Eco/Marine Tourism Development","Development of recreational and eco/marine tourism (with Tourism Authority);",""]],"10":[[1,"64","4","International Forest Conservation Financing Mechanism","we need to seek an international financial mechanism to encourage us to preserve these forests.",""],[1,"64","4","Onshore Log Processing Requirement","PNG needs to move to only allow onshore processing of logs as soon as possible.",""],[1,"67","6","Ban on Export of Old-Growth Logging","Banning the export of old growth logging;",""],[1,"67","7","Domestic Log and Forest Product Processing Initiative","Processing of logs and forest products within the country to generate income and employment;",""],[1,"67","8","Afforestation and Reforestation Programme","Maintaining areas under forest cover through afforestation/reforestation;",""],[1,"67","9","Carbon Trading for Landowner Income","Increasing the income of landowners through carbon trading;",""],[1,"67","10","Expansion of National Parks and Protected Areas","Increasing areas under national parks and protected areas to protect biodiversity;",""]],"11":[[1,"76","5","Tourism Sector Development through Cultural and Eco-Tourism Promotion","The MTDP2 aims at developing the tourism sector through the promotion of cultural and eco-tourism as well as research on culture, biodiversity and medicinal plants.",""]],"12":[[1,"48","2","Tuition Fee-Free Education Policy","the Government has made a considerable commitment to education through the introduction of the Tuition Fee-Free Education policy for students at elementary, primary and secondary school levels.",""],[1,"48","3","Teacher Recruitment and Training Support","The Government is providing financial support to recruit new teachers and improve teacher training, improve the national curriculum and examinations standards and provide school curriculum materials and equipment.",""],[1,"48","3","District Education Infrastructure Funding Model","At the sub-national level the new District Education Infrastructure funding model (2015 Budget) is allowing District administrators to address the backlog of school infrastructure needs.",""],[1,"49","8","Education Sector Expenditure Support","This level of support will continue under MTDP2.",""]],"13":[[1,"49","7","Scholarship Expansion Programme","The Government recognizes the need for universities and colleges to step-up and meet this demand and is responding by increasing the number of scholarships;",""],[1,"49","7","Student Loan Scheme Reintroduction","re- introducing the student loan scheme;",""],[1,"49","7","Higher Learning and Training Institution Expansion","increasing the number of new higher learning and training institutions as well as the capacity in existing institutions.",""],[1,"49","7","Post-secondary Institutional Infrastructure Rehabilitation","the Government is significantly rehabilitating post-secondary institutional infrastructure, most of which was built in the 1970s.",""]],"14":[[1,"7","3","Medium Term Development Plan 2016-2017","I was proud to launch the National Strategy for Responsible Sustainable Development, or StaRS, in Alotau on the 31st of March 2014, and now the Medium Term Development Plan2 2016-2017 (MTDP2).",""],[1,"9","6","National Planning and Service Delivery Frameworks Establishment","The Bill establishes the National Planning Framework, the National Service Delivery Framework (NSDF) and the Monitoring and Evaluation Framework.",""],[1,"11","1","Cultural and Institutional Reform of the Department of Planning and Monitoring","the Department of Planning and Monitoring is undergoing a series of cultural and institutional reforms","Department of Planning and Monitoring"],[1,"11","3","Integration of StaRS Principles into Development Plans","Embed the StaRS principles into Sector and Provincial plans and ensure that they inform all other development planning;",""],[1,"11","12","Principle-Centred Sustainable Development Framework","Hence we commit ourselves to this new paradigm of principle centred sustainable development, as set out in the MTDP2.",""],[1,"14","1","Responsible Sustainable Development Planning Framework","Responsible Sustainable Development (StaRS) which prescribes new guiding principles for development planning.",""],[1,"14","3","Critical Activity Matrix Implementation","This will be achieved by continuing to focus on the Government's sixteen critical activities identified under its Critical Activity Matrix.",""],[1,"14","10","National Planning and Monitoring Framework Establishment","The Papua New Guinea Planning Bill will give effect to planning and monitoring processes.",""],[1,"15","12","Medium-Term Development Plan 2 Strategic Planning Framework","The MTDP2 will be a useful tool for Governments and administrations preparing development plans and budgets.",""],[1,"17","1","Planning, Implementation and Monitoring Cycle","The Department of National Planning and Monitoring (DNPM) is formalizing the national planning and monitoring activities of the Government through the introduction of the Planning, Implementation and Monitoring (PIM) Cycle.","Department of National Planning and Monitoring (DNPM)"],[1,"26","2","Implementation of the Government's Critical Activity Matrix","The MTDP2 will focus on the sixteen critical activities contained in the Government's Critical Activity Matrix as the blueprint for the O'Neill/Dion Governments development actions.",""],[1,"27","1","Service Delivery Standards Support","It also provides advice and support in meeting new service delivery standards and establishing the NSDF.",""],[1,"29","1","National Spatial Development Framework Support for PIM Cycle Implementation","The NSDF supports the Implementation step of the PIM Cycle.",""],[1,"39","1","National Spatial Development Framework Coordination","All development partners are being encouraged to understand and co-ordinate efforts towards building the NSDF.",""],[1,"83","16","DNPM Agency Liaison and M&E Monitoring","Under the MTDP2 officers from DNPM will regularly liaise with agencies to monitor the progress of their M&E activities.",""],[1,"83","16","DNPM Data Collection Training","The DNPM will also organize training on data collection",""],[1,"84","1","Sector Agency Monitoring and Evaluation Capacity Strengthening","and analysis to strengthen the M&E capacity of sector agencies.",""],[1,"84","8","Development Review, Assessment, and Evaluation Collaboration","The DNPM will work together with development partners and implementing agencies in these areas.",""]],"15":[[1,"44","8","Political Parties and Candidates Integrity Act Amendment","Amending the Integrity of Political Parties and Candidates Act to improve political stability and accountability of the Parliament;",""],[1,"44","9","Independent Commission Against Corruption Bill","Introducing the Independent Commission Against Corruption Bill to improve the integrity of public administration among public sector organizations in the country by exposing corruption and corrupt practices;",""],[1,"60","5","Repeal of Prior Parliamentary Legislation","Repealing the legislation passed in the last Parliament (Judicial Conduct Act, Supreme Court Amendment Act, Parliamentary Privileges and Immunities Act);",""],[1,"60","6","Inter-Agency Committee Against Corruption","Establishing, on an ongoing basis, the Inter-Agency Committee Against Corruption;",""],[1,"60","7","Independent Commission Against Corruption Bill","Introducing the Independent Commission Against Corruption Bill in Parliament",""]],"16":[[1,"15","1","National Services Delivery Framework","The National Services Delivery Framework will establish minimum basic core services requirements for all levels of government and introduce a Service Delivery Centre network that will be based on population distribution and geography.",""],[1,"15","2","Sub-national Service Delivery Devolution Framework","It also aligns our planning processes with the Government's sub-national empowerment policy of devolved responsibility for service delivery, from national departments to provincial, district and local governments and administrators.",""],[1,"15","6","Sub-national Empowerment Policy and Local Government Funding Increase","Moving forward with the sub-national empowerment policy and increasing Province, District and Local Government funding under the PSIP, DSIP and LLGSIP;",""],[1,"27","8","Legislative Framework for National Service Delivery Requirements","It will also provide a legislative basis for the Government's national service delivery requirements and set the minimum level of service delivery and outputs needed from agencies and development partners to roll out its operational strategy.",""],[1,"27","10","National Service Delivery Framework","The DNPM has developed a framework for delivering services across the nation.",""],[1,"29","4","National Services and Infrastructure Provision and Maintenance","The National Government will be responsible for the provision and maintenance of national services and infrastructure (for example, education and health infrastructure, and national roads);",""],[1,"29","5","Subnational Delivery of Basic Goods and Services","Provinces, Districts and Wards will be responsible for the delivery of goods and services at their respective levels (for example, rural class rooms, Aid Posts and local roads);",""],[1,"29","6","Regional and Local Government Headquarters Linkage System","Regional Service Centres will be linked to Provincial Headquarters and District Headquarters will be linked to LLG Headquarters, Ward Zone Headquarters and Ward Headquarters;",""],[1,"29","8","New Service Delivery Centres Establishment","New Service Delivery Centres will be established based on spatial distribution (population and other demographic features of an area) and connected by transport and communication links.",""],[1,"39","3","Strategic Service Delivery Centre Coordination Framework","Against this framework of minimum services delivered at strategic service delivery centres, attempts are being made to better co-ordinate and focus the efforts of all stakeholders to improve outcomes.",""],[1,"39","6","Subnational Government Empowerment through Service Improvement and Functional Grants","Subnational Government empowerment is a major theme with record funding being provided through the Service Improvement Program and increased functional grants, together with supporting financial delegate powers and ceilings.",""],[1,"39","7","District Development Authorities Establishment","To strengthen district administration and streamline processes and practices to improve rollout of services at the district and ward level, the Government has also recently established the District Development Authorities (DDAs).",""],[1,"39","8","District Development Authority Service Delivery and Local Planning Reform","The DDAs commenced in January 2015 and will replace the Joint District Planning and Budget Priority Committees.",""],[1,"39","9","Service Delivery Framework for Basic Infrastructure Planning","The new Service Delivery Framework will identify the infrastructure needed for ensuring citizens have access to the minimum level of services needed to improve quality of life.",""],[1,"40","2","National Planning Legislation for Core Service Standards","The proposed National Planning legislation provides a way forward for achieving this outcome by establishing minimum basic core service requirements for all levels of Government.",""]],"17":[[1,"15","11","Sovereign Wealth Fund Establishment","Establishing the Sovereign Wealth Fund to manage mineral sector revenue and to insulate the PNG economy and the National Budget from commodity volatility.",""],[1,"36","15","Sovereign Wealth Fund Establishment","The SWF is being established to manage the revenue from the LNG and mineral sector with a view to insulating the PNG economy and the budget from volatility and to provide intergenerational equity.",""],[1,"37","2","Sovereign Wealth Fund for Resource Revenue Conversion","the SWF is set up to convert nonrenewable assets into a sustainable and perpetual income stream into the future.",""],[1,"37","3","PNG Sovereign Wealth Fund Governance Framework","There will be a single governance framework for the PNG SWF, but it incorporates two funds - a Stabilization Fund and a Savings Fund.",""],[1,"37","3","PNG Stabilization Fund","The Stabilization Fund will reduce the impact of fluctuating mineral and petroleum revenues on the PNG economy and on the budget",""],[1,"37","3","PNG Savings Fund","the Savings Fund will provide a means of preserving the real value of extracted mineral and petroleum resources through long-term investment for the benefit of future generations of PNG.",""],[1,"37","7","Natural Resource Revenue Asset Management Support","Support asset management in relation to financial assets accrued from natural resources revenue.",""],[1,"37","8","Offshore Sovereign Wealth Fund Operations","PNG's offshore Sovereign Wealth Fund (SWF) is expected to commence operations by 2016.",""],[1,"44","13","Sovereign Wealth Fund Organic Law","Establishing the Organic Law on the Sovereign Wealth Fund to manage the revenue from the LNG and mineral sector with a view to insulating the PNG economy and the budget from volatility and to provide intergenerational equity;",""],[1,"64","1","Sovereign Wealth Fund for Mineral and Petroleum Revenues","Carefully harvested, non-renewable mineral and petroleum assets, under an improved fiscal regime including a sovereign wealth fund, can fund our capital deficit (stabilization fund) and provide investments to maintain that capital in the future (savings fund).",""],[1,"73","9","Sovereign Wealth Fund Establishment","Establishing the Sovereign Wealth Fund to protect benefits for the current and future generations;",""],[1,"74","9","Sovereign Wealth Fund Establishment","Establishing of the Sovereign Wealth Fund to provide equitable benefits for the current and future generations;",""]],"18":[[1,"59","1","Sports Infrastructure Upgrade for Pacific Games","a special intervention is being made to upgrade sports infrastructure because of the 2015 Pacific Games.",""]],"19":[[1,"14","9","Modern Contraceptive Access Expansion","One example of the Government addressing this issue will be investing in programs and activities during 2016-2017 that increases the availability of modern contraceptives to PNG couples.",""],[1,"25","12","Public-Private Partnership Expansion for Family Planning Services","Under the MTDP2 the Government will expand its public/private partnerships to further improve access to family planning services, specifically targeted at improving the length of time couples use contraception.",""],[1,"25","14","Family Planning Promotion and Birth Rate Reduction Initiative","Under the MTDP2, relevant agencies and organizations in the health, education and law & justice sectors will be required to take on the important role of promoting family planning and reducing the overall birth rate.",""],[1,"45","8","National Population Policy Reintroduction","Reintroducing the National Population Policy to stabilize population growth;",""],[1,"50","11","Family Planning Service Provision","Provision of family planning is an important component of the service in the health sector.",""],[1,"63","5","National Contraception Access and Family Planning Empowerment","Initially PNG should empower every family and every citizen with the knowledge and access to contraception and begin the process of breaking the poverty cycle at individual and family level.",""]],"20":[[1,"51","12","Long-Term Infrastructure Delivery Financing and Implementation Mechanism","It is intended that modalities for delivery of major infrastructure are informed by historic experience and funding and technical arrangements such as Civil Aviation Development Investment Program on airport infrastructure development are utilized to give long term funding and implementation capacity and certainty.",""],[1,"51","12","Dedicated National Highways Delivery Unit","Road infrastructure for example for the national highways should be delivered by a dedicated technical unit under the Department of Works where all funding is combined into a comprehensive 5 to 10 year outlook.","Department of Works"],[1,"52","4","Integrated Transport System Improvement","To deliver an effective and well-coordinated transport system the Government is committed to improving three modes of transport; air, sea/ waterways and land.",""],[1,"52","6","National and Provincial Road Infrastructure Expansion","Re-building key road infrastructure will continue under MTDP2.",""],[1,"52","7","Road Durability and Maintenance Programme","the Government will continue its emphasis on road durability (sustainability) and maintenance.",""],[1,"52","12","Road Infrastructure Maintenance Programme","Maintaining the value of existing investments in road infrastructure through an emphasis on maintenance;",""],[1,"52","13","Integrated Road Construction and Maintenance Contracting","Encouraging a quality-based focus on new road construction through integrated construction and maintenance contracting arrangements;",""],[1,"52","14","Development of Industry Standards for Durable Road Construction","Encouraging the development of industry standards on long lasting and appropriate durable materials and methodologies to improve road construction reliability;",""],[1,"52","15","Local Road Construction and Maintenance Capacity Policy","Developing policies to grow the capacity of local industry to build and sustainably maintain completed roads; and",""],[1,"52","16","Road Safety Infrastructure Improvement","Improving road safety infrastructures.",""]],"21":[[1,"53","16","Port Development Program","Under the MTDP2, the Government will continue its Port Development program.",""],[1,"53","17","Port Capacity Expansion in Lae and Port Moresby","Increasing the capacity of ports in Lae and Port Moresby to support economic growth and particularly export industries;",""],[1,"54","1","Maintenance Dredging for Smaller Non-Commercial Ports","Rehabilitating infrastructure and in particular undertaking maintenance dredging for smaller non-commercial ports to ensure ongoing serviceability;",""],[1,"54","2","Inland River and Coastal Jetties Infrastructure Improvement","Improving inland river and coastal infrastructure such as jetties to support service delivery.",""],[1,"54","4","Maritime Regulatory and Safety Function Consolidation","Consolidating the maritime regulatory and safety functions to deliver better and more consistent services to the maritime sector;",""],[1,"54","5","Marine Industry Advisory Group","Establishing the Marine Industry Advisory Group to enhance public/private relationships across the maritime sector.",""],[1,"54","6","Maritime Transport System Improvement","An improved maritime transport system will ensure greater access and efficiency within the maritime transport sector.",""],[1,"54","7","Container Storage and Freight Movement Improvement","With the introduction of 20 and 40 foot container storage facilities at all international and local port terminals and freight movement to remote areas including inland waterways, the turnabout time will be reduced to 2.5 days by 2017.",""]],"22":[[1,"43","1","Remote Airstrip Maintenance through Rural Airstrips Authority","The maintenance of remote airstrips by third level airlines through the newly established Rural Airstrips Authority is also an example of utilizing government funding to deliver services through established and committed partners.",""],[1,"54","17","Airport Certification and Compliance System","The Government has adopted a system of certification that requires airports to achieve and maintain compliance with minimum international operating standards.",""],[1,"55","2","Airport Expansion Programme","Expanding Port Moresby International Airport (both airside facilities and terminal) as well as regional airports in the country to accommodate expected increases in tourism and business activity;",""],[1,"55","3","Air Transport Infrastructure Maintenance","Ensuring the maintenance of existing air transport infrastructure;",""],[1,"55","4","Safety and Security Standards Improvement and Maintenance","Improve and maintain safety and security standards meeting international benchmarks;",""],[1,"55","5","Rural Airstrip Rehabilitation Programme","Progressively rehabilitating rural airstrips to help develop rural air services.",""],[1,"55","6","Airport Sustainability Improvement","the Government will focus on improving sustainability of existing airports and the air services that use them.",""],[1,"55","7","Major Airport Commercial Viability Assessment","Undertaking an assessment of the commercial viability of all major airports including alternative revenue sources and appropriate funding strategies to ensure their sustainability;",""],[1,"55","8","Provincial Airports and Rural Airstrips Management and Funding Plan","Developing a plan for the effective management and funding of Provincial airports and rural airstrips;",""],[1,"55","9","Air Transport Infrastructure Expansion and Maintenance","Expanding, improving and maintaining existing air transport infrastructure.",""]],"23":[[1,"58","13","ICT Infrastructure Development for Cost-Efficient Public and Private Services","The Government's objective under its ICT policy is to provide cost efficient, reliable and effective ICT services through the development of ICT infrastructure in the public and private sector.",""]],"24":[[1,"45","9","Water and Sanitation Health Policy Development","Developing the Water and Sanitation Health Policy in addition to the PNG Aid Policy to increase access to reliable and affordable water and sanitation services.",""],[1,"56","4","WaSH Policy 2015-2030","The Government recognizes that greater effort is needed to achieve its water and sanitation objectives and has launched the WaSH Policy 2015-2030.",""],[1,"56","7","Management Information System Development and Management","3. Develop and manage an effective management information system,",""],[1,"56","12","WaSH Policy Implementation","The Government's strong expectation is that implementing the WaSH Policy 2015-2030 will contribute to achieving health targets and improving the country's HDI ranking.",""],[1,"70","6","Water Resources Strategic Policy and Action Plan Development and Implementation","Development of strategic policy and action plan on the water resources and its implementation;",""],[1,"70","7","Improved Water Source Access Expansion","Increasing the access of rural and urban households and schools and health institutions on improved water source;",""]],"25":[[1,"14","3","Expenditure and Revenue Reforms","These activities will deliver expenditure and revenue reforms;",""],[1,"26","2","Fiscal Resource Mobilization and Implementation Strategy","It will continue its fiscal strategy of ensuring the Government's fiscal plans are adequately resourced and implemented in a manner that is innovative, practical and efficient.",""],[1,"27","1","Resource Mobilization and Procurement Innovation","It sets out how the Government is undertaking the critical activities of maximizing resources and improving and innovating implementation and procurement.",""],[1,"33","4","Revenue Mobilization and Public Finance Reform Program","To support this step up in expenditure, the Government has put in place a program of policy and legislative reforms to maximize government resources.",""],[1,"34","7","Legislative and Policy Revenue Mobilization Package","The Government's budget strategy is supported by a program of legislative and policy interventions that maximize government resourcing.",""],[1,"34","9","Revenue Generation and Collection Strengthening","A greater emphasis on revenue generation and collection in the budgetary process, including greater scrutiny over Statutory Authorities and Government Corporations dividend policy;",""],[1,"34","10","Revenue Collection Capacity Strengthening for IRC and Customs","Improving the capacity of IRC and Customs to better collect government revenues;",""],[1,"34","11","Tax Review for Tax Administration Improvement","Establishing the Tax Review to improve tax collection systems and processes with the aim of broadening the tax base;",""],[1,"35","1","Taxpayer Registration Expansion Measures","Increasing the number of taxpayers by introducing series of measures that required participants to submit tax file numbers;",""],[1,"36","7","Equitable Taxation and Taxpayer Compliance Regime","Maintaining an equitable taxation regime, with a focus on taxpayer compliance;",""],[1,"36","8","Tax Exemption and Special Tax Arrangement Limitation","Limiting the categories of taxation exemptions and special taxation arrangements.",""],[1,"44","15","IRC Statutory Authority Conversion","Converting the IRC to a Statutory Authority to improve the operational efficiency of the organization and its tax collection role;",""],[1,"44","16","Tax Review for Revenue Administration Improvement","Conducting the Tax Review to improve the collection systems and processes and to broaden the tax base.",""]],"26":[[1,"7","5","Planning Act to Link Medium-Term Development Plans and National Budgets","It elevates the principles of responsible development and prescribes a planning act to link MTDPs and the underlying development principles to national budgets.",""],[1,"9","5","Papua New Guinea Planning Act","The proposed Papua New Guinea Planning Act, which we are presenting with this MTDP2, links the planning process to annual National Budgets through progressive MTDPs.",""],[1,"15","5","Medium-Term Fiscal Strategy Debt and Deficit Targeting","Setting debt and deficit targets under the Medium Term Fiscal Strategy to provide ongoing private sector confidence in the Government's fiscal position and return the National Budget to balance by 2017;",""],[1,"26","5","Legislative Planning and Monitoring Framework","For the first time, the MTDP2 will sit within the broader planning framework described under the proposed legislation.",""],[1,"27","5","National Planning Act and Planning Framework Institutionalization","The proposed National Planning Act will link the long and medium term plans to the annual budget and establish the NSDF and Monitoring and Evaluation Framework.",""],[1,"27","6","National Planning Act Legislative Framework","The proposed National Planning Act will put in place the legislative framework needed to support the new national planning and monitoring structure.",""],[1,"27","7","Development Principles and Planning-Implementation-Monitoring Cycle Legislation","The proposed legislation will clarify and embed the development principles, establish the Planning, Implementation and Monitoring Cycle with respective supporting frameworks and connect the MTDPs to the annual budgets.",""],[1,"29","9","National Planning Act","The proposed National Planning Act will provide the legal basis for the framework.",""],[1,"34","6","Five-Year Fiscal Regime for Borrowing and Resource Mobilization","The Government has deliberately gone about maximizing its resource envelope within prudent guidelines by determining a five year outlook and fiscal regime to utilize borrowings on the back of the PNG LNG Project to fund these activities at record allocations.",""],[1,"35","2","Fiscal Responsibility Act Amendment","Amending the Fiscal Responsibility Act 2006 to increase the allowable budget deficit and debt to GDP ratios;",""],[1,"35","6","Medium Term Fiscal Strategy","The Medium Term Fiscal Strategy (MTFS) allows the Government to maintain macroeconomic stability and investor confidence, while supporting government's high levels of capital expenditure directed at creating the enabling environment for private sector led growth.",""],[1,"35","9","Expenditure Program Monitoring and Fiscal Discipline","the Government will monitor its expenditure program to ensure it is consistent with the evolving economic and fiscal situation.",""],[1,"36","13","Budget Deficit Reduction and Balance Restoration","For deficit management the guiding principle is to return the Budget to expenditure/ revenue balance by 2017.",""],[1,"44","11","Fiscal Responsibility Act Amendments","Amendments to the Fiscal Responsibility Act have also been undertaken to enable major investment and improve service delivery.",""],[1,"44","12","Medium Term Fiscal Strategy","Introducing the Medium Term Fiscal Strategy to enable the Government to properly plan, resource and implement its intervention Programs;",""],[1,"44","14","Public Financial Management Act Amendment","Amending the Public Financial Management Act to improve the management of public finances - revenue and expenditures;",""],[1,"45","7","National Planning Legislation Drafting","Drafting the National Planning legislation to underpin the Government's national planning and monitoring framework;",""]],"27":[[1,"15","14","Quarterly and Annual Results Monitoring and Reporting System","under the MTDP2, they need to monitor their inputs/budgets and outputs/outcomes on a quarterly and annual basis and submit them to DNPM for consolidation and reporting to Government.",""],[1,"27","4","Monitoring and Evaluation Support for Agencies","Under Chapter five agencies are supported to undertake monitoring and evaluation activities - an important component of the MTDP2.",""],[1,"29","10","Monitoring and Evaluation Policy and National Strategy for Statistics","The Monitoring and Evaluation Framework is being finalized through an M&E policy and a National Strategy for Statistics at the DNPM.",""],[1,"29","11","MTDP Tracking Pocketbook","The proposed Planning Act establishes the MTDP Tracking Pocketbook to report on an annual basis on the MTDP indicators, the Critical Activity Matrix (CAM) to identify and track the top sixteen program activities of Government and the Public Investment Program reports to track all investment activities of government, supported by all other reporting requirements of government.",""],[1,"29","11","Critical Activity Matrix","The proposed Planning Act establishes the MTDP Tracking Pocketbook to report on an annual basis on the MTDP indicators, the Critical Activity Matrix (CAM) to identify and track the top sixteen program activities of Government and the Public Investment Program reports to track all investment activities of government, supported by all other reporting requirements of government.",""],[1,"29","11","Public Investment Program Reporting System","The proposed Planning Act establishes the MTDP Tracking Pocketbook to report on an annual basis on the MTDP indicators, the Critical Activity Matrix (CAM) to identify and track the top sixteen program activities of Government and the Public Investment Program reports to track all investment activities of government, supported by all other reporting requirements of government.",""],[1,"29","13","Monitoring and Evaluation Support for the PIM Cycle","The NMEF supports the Monitoring and Evaluation step in the PIM Cycle.",""],[1,"31","1","Agency Development Program Monitoring and Reporting Requirement","particularly those involved in the health, education, infrastructure, strategic assets, law & justice, data production and National ID development will be required to monitor the inputs, outputs and outcomes of their development programs.",""],[1,"31","1","Quarterly and Annual Progress Reporting to DNPM","Under this MTDP2 agencies will now be required to submit their quarterly and annual progress reports on inputs/budgets, outputs and outcomes to the DNPM for consolidation and reporting to the Government.",""],[1,"31","3","Development Program Monitoring and Evaluation System","Data generated through surveys such as the Demographic and Health Survey, Multiple Indicators Surveys, Censuses, monitoring reports and rapid assessments will become the basis for mid-term reviews and final evaluations of development program.",""]],"29":[[1,"38","7","Development Partner Aid Alignment and Coordination","The Government is committed to maximizing the benefits of this support by ensuring it aligns with PNGs development plans, is better coordinated and visible.",""],[1,"38","8","Advancement of PNG Commitment on Aid Effectiveness Targets","This work will continue in 2015 by advancing the targets agreed in the PNG Commitment on Aid Effectiveness, signed in July 2008.",""],[1,"38","9","Aid Policy Finalization and Donor Program Screening","This will also see the Government finalize its new Aid Policy and allow DNPM to review existing donor partners' assistance to ensure alignment with the new policy approach.",""],[1,"38","9","DNPM Screening of Donor-Supported Programs","The screening by DNPM of all new donor supported programs, which began in 2014 with the re-institutionalization and strengthening of the PIP guidelines, will continue.","DNPM"],[1,"38","10","Annual Aid Report Reintroduction","This work will be supported by the Government's re-introduction of the Annual Aid Report, which will further improve transparency and accountability of donor grants into the future.",""],[1,"38","11","Strategic Use of Consultants and Advisors in Capacity Development Programs","particular attention is also being paid to the strategic use of consultants/advisors in long-term management and capacity development programs, with the view to reducing the level of assistance as a percentage of foreign aid over time.",""],[1,"38","12","Strategic Placement and Screening of Consultants and Advisors","Consultants/Advisors will be strategically placed in appropriate locations.",""],[1,"38","13","National and Sector Dialogue with Development Partners","The Government will continue to strengthen national and sector dialogue with its development partners through its biannual donor forums and ongoing funding of the Development Assistance Database.",""]],"30":[[1,"15","8","Innovative Procurement and Public-Private Partnership Access Initiative","Facilitating innovative procurement strategies, including public/private partnerships, to improve access to goods and services at the local level;",""],[1,"44","4","Private Sector Partnership for Infrastructure Expansion","Encouraging private sector partnerships to gain access to the skills, technology and finance that are needed to improve performance and expand infrastructure.",""],[1,"45","3","Public-Private Partnership Legislation Amendment","Amending the Public Private Partnership Legislation Act to create an enabling platform for effective partnership between Government and the private sector to improve service delivery;",""]],"31":[[1,"42","8","Church Partnership Program Financial Support","One example of this approach is the financial support provided to faith based organizations through the Church Partnership Program to deliver health and education services.",""]],"32":[[1,"35","3","PNG LNG Gas Project Delivery Support","Supporting the early delivery of the PNG LNG Gas Project and subsequent additional trains, and a second major gas project and other projects.",""],[1,"35","3","Additional Gas Trains Expansion","Supporting the early delivery of the PNG LNG Gas Project and subsequent additional trains, and a second major gas project and other projects.",""],[1,"35","3","Second Major Gas Project Development","Supporting the early delivery of the PNG LNG Gas Project and subsequent additional trains, and a second major gas project and other projects.",""],[1,"74","3","Petroleum and Gas Institutional Capacity Strengthening","strengthening the institutional capacity of state institutions mandated with the administration of the sector",""],[1,"74","3","Petroleum and Gas Policy and Legislative Review","a review of petroleum & gas policies and supporting legislation to address the findings of the taxation review and adopting the StaRS",""],[1,"74","3","Stakeholder Engagement Mechanism for Landowner Concerns","developing adequate stakeholder engagement mechanisms to address landowner concerns",""],[1,"74","5","Strengthening State Institutions for Policy and Enforcement","Strengthening state institutions responsible for policy, administration, regulation, compliance and enforcement;",""],[1,"74","7","Continued Exploration Investment","Encouraging continued investment in exploration;",""],[1,"74","10","Oil and Gas Act Review","Reviewing of the Oil & Gas Act to capture the recommendations from the tax review and adopting principles of sustainable development;",""],[1,"74","11","Downstream Petroleum and Gas Processing Facilitation","Facilitating downstream processing for petroleum and gas products;",""]],"33":[[1,"59","6","PNG-Australia Law and Justice Partnership","This includes the PNG-Australia Law and Justice Partnership, Waigani Court House Complex and an increase in the number of Judges and Court circuits held in Provinces and Districts.",""],[1,"59","6","Waigani Court House Complex","This includes the PNG-Australia Law and Justice Partnership, Waigani Court House Complex and an increase in the number of Judges and Court circuits held in Provinces and Districts.",""],[1,"59","6","Expansion of Judges and Court Circuits","This includes the PNG-Australia Law and Justice Partnership, Waigani Court House Complex and an increase in the number of Judges and Court circuits held in Provinces and Districts.",""],[1,"59","6","Village Court Officials Allowance Funding","In 2015 Budget the Government fully funded allowances for village court officials.",""]],"34":[[1,"81","7","National Statistical Data Collection and Reporting Support","Under MTDP2 the Government will provide necessary funding to NSO for this purpose.",""],[1,"81","9","NSO Reporting Capacity Support","To improve the reporting capability of the NSO the Government has provided necessary financial support, including:",""],[1,"81","10","National Electronic ID Program","Introducing the National ID Program to provide unique electronic ID to all PNG citizens to improve service delivery;",""],[1,"81","11","Civil Registration and National Statistics Institutional Merger","Delegating the Civil Registration System (CRS) to the DNPM and amalgamating the CRS and NSO to eventually form the Bureau of Civil Registry and National Statistics;",""],[1,"81","12","Population Information System Establishment","Establishing the Population Information System",""],[1,"82","1","National Statistics Office Overhaul and Capacity Building Reform","The Government has recognized the need to overhaul the NSO with reinvigorated legislation, structure and management.",""],[1,"82","2","Multi-Year Action Plan for NSO Reform","the formulation of a multi- year Action Plan to address these issues following a review with the support of the IMF and the Australian Bureau of Statistics;",""],[1,"82","4","Secretariat Establishment","Setting up a Secretariat to be run by the Department of Treasury and including the DNPM;","Department of Treasury | DNPM"],[1,"82","6","Joint National Planning and Treasury NEC Submission for NSO Overhaul","Preparing a joint National Planning/Treasury NEC Submission outlining the final plans for overhauling the NSO.",""],[1,"82","9","Civil Registry and National Statistics Bureau Formation","In order to improve performance on data, the Government will amalgamate the CRS and NSO to eventually form the Bureau of Civil Registry and National Statistics during the MTDP2 period.",""],[1,"82","10","Population Information System Establishment","The PIS will be established at the reformed National Statistics Office.",""],[1,"83","14","National Electronic ID and Population Information System","The objective of the program is to provide unique electronic ID to all PNG citizens to assist them to obtain access to public goods and services more efficiently.",""],[1,"83","14","Provincial Civil Registry Office Expansion","This program will also involve the establishment of permanent offices in every province under the Civil Registry Office where NSO and Planning staff can also be located.",""]],"38":[[1,"40","4","Ward-Level Community Health Post and Aid Post Provision","each Council Ward must have at least one Community Health Post or Aid Post.",""],[1,"50","3","Community-Level Health Service Delivery Expansion","Continuously expanding health service delivery at the community level through the following structure:",""],[1,"51","9","Upgrade Sub Health Centres and Aid Posts","The Government aims at gradually upgrading Sub Health Centres into Health Centres and some Aid Posts into Community Health Posts.",""]],"39":[[1,"14","3","Implementation and Procurement Practice Innovation","and innovate implementation and procurement practices.",""],[1,"15","3","Public Resourcing, Implementation, and Procurement Reforms","The MTDP2 will be supported by important reforms in public resourcing, implementation and procurement, which are already contributing to the necessary enabling environment.",""],[1,"36","5","Project Design and Full Costing Requirement","Funding new infrastructure projects only after the proposal has been properly designed and fully costed.",""],[1,"42","1","Public Finance Management Act Reform for CSTB Transparency","The initial task is the required reforms to the Public Finance Management Act to improve the effectiveness and transparency of the Central Supplies & Tenders Board (CSTB).",""],[1,"42","2","CSTB Procurement Reform","reforms are required to improve transparency and independence of the Board and to separate functions such as that of the State Solicitor.",""],[1,"42","3","Independent Health Procurement Authority","The Government has mooted the Independent Health Procurement Authority and this should be progressed more rapidly.",""],[1,"42","4","Strengthening Provincial and District Procurement and Works Units","Provincial Governments must have functioning Provincial Supply and Tenders Boards and Provincial Works Units.",""],[1,"42","5","Public Procurement Reform","The Government will amend the legislation and issue non-financial instructions to improve and speed up procurement at both the national and sub national government level.",""],[1,"42","6","Tender Approval Process Guidelines","the Government has commissioned the CSTB to draft a set of clear guidelines on the tender approval process, including the length of time required for each stage of the process.",""],[1,"43","2","Procurement System Review and Improvement","Under the MTDP2 work will continue to review and improve the procurement system so that public goods and services can reach PNG citizens in a timely and cost effective manner.",""],[1,"45","2","Public Procurement Policy and Practice Review","Reviewing public Procurement policies and practices to improve and speed up procurement at both the national and sub national levels of government so that services can get to the people in a timely and cost effective manner;",""],[1,"52","11","Two-Stage Business Case Project Appraisal Reform","Improving the assessment of major rehabilitation and new construction projects using a two staged Business Case approach to ensure value for money and enhanced socioeconomic returns for the people of Papua New Guinea;",""]],"40":[[1,"15","9","State-Owned Enterprise Reform","Reforming State Owned Enterprises to improve revenue returns and enhance competition;",""],[1,"35","4","State-Owned Enterprise Competition and Privatization Policy Reform","Amending legislation to improve State Owned Enterprise competition and enhance its privatization policy;",""],[1,"36","4","Public Administration and Governance Improvement","Improving agencies' public administration and governance arrangement by focusing on expenditure efficiencies, transparency of activity reporting and better public accountability;",""],[1,"43","4","Public Sector Restructuring and Administrative Reform","introducing the Rightsizing Initiative and the Service Improvement Program to restructure the public sector and improve administrative processes; and roll-out of manpower and payroll audits to remove discrepancies and salary over-runs.",""],[1,"43","4","Public Service Management Act Amendment","amendments to the Public Service Management Act 2014;",""],[1,"43","4","Manpower and Payroll Audit Roll-out","roll-out of manpower and payroll audits to remove discrepancies and salary over-runs.",""],[1,"43","6","Budget Management Framework Reform","the Government announced the reform of the Budget Management Framework with the introduction of the Consolidated Budget Operating Rules to assist agencies to manage their budget expenditure, during the year and in the preparation of Budget submissions.",""],[1,"43","7","Public Sector Efficiency Review","the Government has announced an efficiency review of the public sector.",""],[1,"43","8","Legislative and Administrative Public Sector Reform","Under MTDP2, the Government will continue to initiate its legislative and administrative reforms to improve public sector efficiencies during 2016-2017 and beyond.",""],[1,"43","9","State-Owned Enterprise Commercialization Reform","The Government's policy objectives in relation to State Owned Enterprises (SOEs) is to reform them to operate as commercial entities",""],[1,"44","2","State-Owned Enterprise Efficiency and Privatization Reform","For the Government to create the best environment for service delivery and infrastructure development through increasing the efficiency of SOEs, privatization in appropriate cases and constructive partnerships with the private sector.",""],[1,"44","3","State-Owned Enterprise Competition and Efficiency Reform","Supporting competition, to encourage SOEs to become more efficient and identify when the private sector can provide quality services at a lower cost;",""],[1,"44","10","Public Service Management Act Amendment for Appointment Streamlining","Amending the Public Service Management Act to streamline government appointments.",""],[1,"45","5","Independent Consumer and Competition Commission Act Review","Reviewing the Independent Consumer & Competition Commission Act to ensure competition, fair trading and consumer protection;",""]],"41":[[1,"29","7","Minimum Basic Core Service Requirements for Health Facilities","Minimum basic core service requirements will be introduced (for example, clean running water in health facilities);",""],[1,"49","12","Health System Strengthening and Service Delivery Improvement","The Government's long-term plan is to provide an efficient and effective health system that delivers internationally acceptable standard of health services across PNG.",""],[1,"50","9","Regional Specialist Hospital Expansion","Expanding of Regional (specialist) hospitals in Lae (Angau), Mt. Hagen, Port Moresby and other centers like Wewak (Boram) and Enga;",""],[1,"50","10","Recruitment and Training of Medical Professionals and Health Workers","Recruitment and training of medical professionals and workers.",""],[1,"50","11","Continuing HIV/AIDS, Malaria, Tuberculosis, Preventive and Noncommunicable Disease Services","The sector will also continuously provide services on HIV/AIDS; malaria and TB; preventative healthcare; and emerging noncommunicable diseases such as diabetes and asthma.",""],[1,"50","12","Health Sector Expenditure Support","This level of support will continue under MTDP2.",""]],"42":[[1,"59","7","Security Sector Modernization Support","The Government is also providing significant financial support to modernize the Police, Defence and Correctional Services and meet the security costs of the 2015 Pacific Games and APEC (Asia-Pacific Economic Cooporation).",""],[1,"60","2","Police Force Modernization","Modernizing the police force;",""],[1,"60","3","Office of the Secretary for Police","Establishing the office of the Secretary for Police to oversee the effective administration and management of the force;",""],[1,"60","4","Police Commissioner Recruitment Process Review","Reviewing the process for recruiting police Commissioners and Deputy Commissioners;",""]],"43":[[1,"60","17","Affordable Land and Housing Program","The Government has recognized the chronic shortage of affordable land and housing in PNG and has adopted the Land and Housing policy.",""],[1,"61","1","Land Reform and Affordable Housing Development Program","Funding provided to this program is supporting the Land Reform Program to progress the mobilization of customary land, institutional housing of at least 10 houses per district, and the capturing of existing alienated land to develop affordable housing.",""],[1,"61","1","Affordable Housing Pilot Allotment Projects","Pilot programs at Duran Farm and Gerehu 3B in Port Moresby will provide 10,000 allotments.",""],[1,"61","2","Free Land Title Pilot for Housing Finance Access","The Gerehu 3B project will pilot the provision of free titles to qualifying Papua New Guineans to access funding provided to commercial banks at 4% interest with 40 year terms.",""],[1,"61","6","Affordable Urban and Institutional Housing Land Access","Increasing access to State and traditional land for affordable housing in urban areas and institutional housing at sub-national level;",""],[1,"61","7","Land Titles System Improvement","Improving access to affordable financing by improving the land titles system and enhancing Government incentive schemes for major banks;",""],[1,"61","7","Government Incentive Schemes for Major Banks","Improving access to affordable financing by improving the land titles system and enhancing Government incentive schemes for major banks;",""],[1,"61","8","Housing Construction Competition and Efficiency Review","Reviewing government policies and practices to encourage greater competition and efficiency in the housing construction industry;",""],[1,"61","9","Department of Lands and Physical Planning Capacity Building","Building the capacity of the Department of Lands and Physical Planning to effectively contribute to the delivery of the program",""],[1,"61","10","Customary Land Development Model Piloting and Advisory Service","Piloting customary land development models using the Incorporated Land Groups as the mechanism and establishing the special land development advisory service;",""],[1,"61","11","Land Group Incorporation and Customary Land Registration Act Implementation","Implementing the Land Group Incorporation (Amendment) Act and the Land Registration (Customary) (Amendment) Act;",""],[1,"61","12","Land Use Planning Scheme","Producing a \"Land Use Planning Scheme\" to guide the use of land that is consistent with the StaRS.",""],[1,"69","7","Land Access Improvement","Improvement of access to land;",""]],"44":[[1,"14","4","Sustainable Economy Transition Framework","The MTDP2 will begin the move toward a more sustainable economy.",""],[1,"14","4","Indicator and Target Development for Economic Enabling Environment","It will introduce the necessary indicators and targets that create the enabling environment to grow the economy while ensuring proper management and use of PNGs strategic assets.",""],[1,"14","6","Strategic Development of Natural Assets","Under the MTDP2 government investment will focus on developing and strategically positioning these assets to meet the needs of current as well as future generations of Papua New Guineans.",""],[1,"45","6","Responsible Sustainable Development Strategy (StaRS)","Adopting the Responsible Sustainable Development Strategy (StaRS) to reinforce the National Goals and Directives Principles of the constitution in guiding all development activities towards a more sustainable pathway;",""],[1,"64","8","National Strategy for Responsible Sustainable Development","The National Strategy for Responsible Sustainable Development (StaRS) sets out the underlying principles supporting the Government's intention to shift its development (operational) strategy from the current 'brown only' growth model, of resource extraction and export, to a more sustainable 'greener' economy.",""]]}});